he parent create persists its local-ID→Jira mapping (apply-time re-resolution of the child create fields from the fresh binding), OR explicitly scope this plan to ordering-only and accept next-pass parent convergence — and reword the Context/Problem/AC accordingly.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.4,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["outbound_fields.py:182 comment 'Omit the key entirely when unbound so _diff_fields skips it (retry next pass)'","outbound_fields.py:218-220 jira_parent_key = binding_store.get_jira_key(local_parent_id) resolved at build time","outbound_mutation_builders.py:123-134 create_fields built once, before any create is dispatched","Plan persists the mapping but never states the child create re-reads it to inject the parent field at apply time"],"finding":"The mechanism orders the parent create before the child and persists a local-ID→Jira mapping, but does not specify how the child create's parent FIELD acquires the parent Jira key within the same pass. The child create's fields are resolved at build time via binding_store.get_jira_key(local_parent_id) (adapters/jira/outbound_fields.py:183,218-220); for an unbound in-pass parent this returns None and the parent field is omitted ('Omit the key entirely when unbound so _diff_fields skips it (retry next pass)'). Ordering alone does not re-populate the already-built child payload, so the parent/child are correctly ORDERED yet the child still lands parentless in that pass unless an apply-time re-resolution step is added.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f5c76a866ba36a7bf","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach §3 (\"require the ordered parent create to complete and persist the parent local-ID-to-Jira mapping before executing the child operation\"); Context/Problem","norm_id":"n41ec59acbd62c10e","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Parent and child both unbound, created in one pass: pare